-# Verification report: walmart-azure-headless 1.5.2
+# Verification report: walmart-azure-headless 1.6.6
+
+## Release 1.6.6
+
+Release 1.6.6 corrects how a refused automatic publication is reported, a defect the client's review of 1.6.5
+named. What a run collects, checks and exports does not change: the page reader, the records, the gates, the
+exports and the publication's own checks are those of 1.6.5. Integration tests show the defect and its correction:
+each new test fails on 1.6.5 and passes on 1.6.6, and the test that shows what did not change passes on both.
+
+| Change | Until 1.6.5 | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| A complete validated run whose automatic publication is refused (for example WARN findings without a recorded reason, a failed integrity check, or pages that did not come from the network on a target that is not a test target) is an error. The refusal is recorded on the run as an `ERROR` event and logged at `ERROR` (`PUBLICATION_REFUSED`, with its reason), the run's `RUN_FINISHED` summary says so (`publication`: `published` false and the reason), and the execution exits 6 (nothing was published). Azure's retry of that execution (the job's `replicaRetryLimit` is 1) finds the occurrence done, sends nothing and exits 6 again (`OCCURRENCE_DONE` names the refusal). The run stays validated, the last published dataset stays published, and `publish --run ID` publishes the run once the cause is resolved | The refusal was logged at `WARN` only and recorded nowhere on the run, and the execution exited 0, so neither documented alert (an `ERROR` line; `RUN_FINISHED` with `exit_code != 0`) fired and a dataset could stay unpublished unnoticed. Azure's retry exited 0 as well | `operations.py` (`after_run`, `_done_occurrence`, `auto_publication_refused`); `tests/integration/test_operations.py::test_a_refused_automatic_publication_is_an_error_with_a_non_zero_exit` (fails on 1.6.5: the line was `WARN`, nothing was recorded, the exit code was 0) and `::test_a_scheduled_run_whose_publication_was_refused_exits_6_also_on_azures_retry` (fails on 1.6.5: the scheduled execution exited 0); `::test_a_complete_run_is_published_and_a_partial_run_never_replaces_it` (unchanged; passes on both) |
+
+## Release 1.6.5
+
+Release 1.6.5 corrects a defect of the independent source check, found when the export of this delivery's live
+census L10 (release 1.6.4) was verified. What a run collects and exports does not change: the page reader, the
+records, the gates and the exports are those of 1.6.4. An offline test on two pages that census stored shows the
+defect and its correction; each new test of the change fails on 1.6.4 and passes on 1.6.5, and the tests that show
+what did not change pass on both. Live results are not recorded here: the delivery's review documents give each
+live stage, the frozen build it ran on and its result.
+
+| Change | Until 1.6.4 | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| The source check (`checks/source_check.py`: `validate-export --run`, and the automated canary on a run's first recorded page) reads the three price layouts that the page reader reads: price lines, nested price objects (`currentPrice`, `wasPrice`, `unitPrice` › `priceString`), and flat display strings (`priceInfo.linePriceDisplay`, `linePrice` or `itemPrice`; `priceInfo.wasPrice` and `priceInfo.unitPrice` as strings). A was-price above the current price is a sale in each layout. A record whose price or unit price differs from its page's, in any layout, is still a mismatch | The check read price lines and nested objects only. A page in the flat layout showed it no price, so a valid record read from it was a mismatch (its regular price, and its unit price when it has one), or was judged on another page that shows the item differently (its URL or image). Live L10 of 2026-11-04 (run `01M6KA3CKYJSD6WDY4TDAAV73Y`): one page, Beauty's "New Arrivals" (`/browse/beauty/new-arrivals/1085666_4427759`), gave the prices of its 50 placements as flat strings; the check reported 21 of the run's 10,301 records as mismatches (19 regular prices, 12 unit prices, 1 URL, 1 image), each equal to that page's own data, and `validate-export --run` exited 6. The canary compares a run's first recorded page in the same way, so a first page in this layout would have stopped a run (exit 6, store held) although its records were right. Of the 1,526 pages stored by the collector's 21 live runs (releases 1.5.0 to 1.6.4), it is the only page with flat price strings | `checks/source_check.py` (`expected_prices`, `flat_text`); `tests/unit/test_flat_price_layout.py` on the authentic pages `tests/captures/listing_pages_20261104_flat/` (the collector's stored copies, with their manifest) and the run's 26 exported records read from the flat page: the prices read, the 26 records verified, the record seen on both pages judged on its own, the canary's comparison, a wrong price or unit price still a mismatch, a flat was-price as a sale (6 tests: fail on 1.6.4); the manifest and the two pages' layouts (pass on both) |
+
+## Release 1.6.4
+
+Release 1.6.4 corrects the defect that stopped this delivery's live census L7 of 2026-11-04 on release 1.6.3. An
+offline test on the page that census stored shows the defect and its correction; each new test of the change
+fails on 1.6.3 and passes on 1.6.4, and the tests that show what did not change pass on both. Live results are
+not recorded here: the delivery's review documents give each live stage, the frozen build it ran on and its
+result. (Until this release the title of this report still named release 1.6.2; its sections were current.)
+
+| Change | Until 1.6.3 | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| The listing's total is the `aggregatedCount` its page reports, and a reported 0 is a total of 0; the page's `count` (the products the page shows, other modules' too) is read only when the page reports no `aggregatedCount`. A listing whose first page reports 0 results and shows none is `EMPTY` ("the listing shows 0 results") once that page's own data names the store and the fulfillment, whatever other modules the page shows; their products are not the listing's and none is recorded. The run goes on. A first page that reports results and shows none still stops the run (`ABNORMAL_RESULT`) | The total was read as `aggregatedCount or count`, so a reported 0 counted as missing and the page's `count` took its place. Live L7 of 2026-11-04 (run `01M6K7HT3XVV8R8CX79P31KMB4`): the Household Essentials link "Bidets" (`/browse/home-improvement/bidets/1072864_1045879_5533759_6108305`) reported 0 Pickup results for store 3891 (`aggregatedCount` 0, its result grid empty) beside an "Available for shipping" carousel of 10 products (`count` 10); 1.6.3 read a total of 10, stopped the run ("the page reports results but shows no product", `ABNORMAL_RESULT`, exit 6, not resumable) and held the store. Of the 343 listing pages stored by this delivery's live runs, it is the only one the change reads differently | `sites/walmart/page_data.py` (`pagination`); `tests/unit/test_empty_pickup_grid.py` (the authentic page `tests/captures/listing_pages_20261104/bidets_page1.html.gz`, the collector's stored copy, and a reported 0 beside other products: fail on 1.6.3; a total above 0, no or a null `aggregatedCount`, 0 and no product, and the synthetic copy's shape: pass on both); `tests/integration/test_coverage_and_assortment.py::test_a_listing_whose_pickup_grid_is_empty_beside_a_shipping_carousel_is_empty_and_the_run_goes_on` (fails on 1.6.3); `::test_a_page_that_reports_results_it_does_not_show_still_stops_the_run` (unchanged; passes on both) |
+
+## Release 1.6.3
+
+Release 1.6.3 corrects three defects that this delivery's live runs of 2026-11-04 found with release 1.6.2: two in
+what a run publishes for a product's UPC and size, found by the delivery's field-by-field reconciliation of the
+live run L5, and one that stopped the live run L6. Offline tests show each defect and its correction: each new test
+of a change fails on 1.6.2 and passes on 1.6.3, and the tests that show what did not change pass on both. Live
+results are not recorded here: the delivery's review documents give each live stage, the frozen build it ran on and
+its result.
+
